From fd06ed1bfc0bc5a9a46bad22d4d9ba17d35a626a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daryl Denson <daryldenson0405@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:38:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] NetworkCapabilities: treat XCAP as mutable and requestable

On certain cellular networks (e.g. T-Mobile 5G NR), Telephony DataNetwork
dynamically removes NET_CAPABILITY_XCAP from the primary cellular data
network when IWLAN is preferred for XCAP. Because NET_CAPABILITY_XCAP was
treated as immutable, ConnectivityService flagged this capability removal
as a bug (am_wtf: lost immutable capabilities).

Add NET_CAPABILITY_XCAP to MUTABLE_CAPABILITIES so ConnectivityService
allows its dynamic removal, and exclude it from NON_REQUESTABLE_CAPABILITIES
so that telephony and apps can continue requesting XCAP.
---
 framework/src/android/net/NetworkCapabilities.java | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/framework/src/android/net/NetworkCapabilities.java b/framework/src/android/net/NetworkCapabilities.java
index 70f7372f14..ba0b8fe1c1 100644
--- a/framework/src/android/net/NetworkCapabilities.java
+++ b/framework/src/android/net/NetworkCapabilities.java
@@ -830,7 +830,8 @@ public final class NetworkCapabilities implements Parcelable {
             (1L << NET_CAPABILITY_NOT_VCN_MANAGED) |
             // The value of NET_CAPABILITY_HEAD_UNIT is 32, which cannot use int to do bit shift,
             // otherwise there will be an overflow. Use long to do bit shift instead.
-            (1L << NET_CAPABILITY_HEAD_UNIT);
+            (1L << NET_CAPABILITY_HEAD_UNIT) |
+            (1L << NET_CAPABILITY_XCAP);
 
     /**
      * Network capabilities that are not allowed in NetworkRequests. This exists because the
@@ -839,13 +840,14 @@ public final class NetworkCapabilities implements Parcelable {
      * can get into a cycle where the NetworkFactory endlessly churns out NetworkAgents that then
      * get immediately torn down because they do not have the requested capability.
      */
-    // Note that as a historical exception, the TRUSTED and NOT_VCN_MANAGED capabilities
+    // Note that as a historical exception, the TRUSTED, NOT_VCN_MANAGED, and XCAP capabilities
     // are mutable but requestable. Factories are responsible for not getting
     // in an infinite loop about these.
     private static final long NON_REQUESTABLE_CAPABILITIES =
             MUTABLE_CAPABILITIES
             & ~(1L << NET_CAPABILITY_TRUSTED)
-            & ~(1L << NET_CAPABILITY_NOT_VCN_MANAGED);
+            & ~(1L << NET_CAPABILITY_NOT_VCN_MANAGED)
+            & ~(1L << NET_CAPABILITY_XCAP);
 
     /**
      * Capabilities that are set by default when the object is constructed.
